      "seed": 1231602053,
      "version": 176,
      "versionNonce": 1905523397,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788597094290,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "After EKS is deployed, configure kubectl from a machine with VPC access (or via VPN/bastion):\n\n# Update kubeconfig (requires VPC network access)\naws eks update-kubeconfig \\\n  --region ap-southeast-1 \\\n  --name hc-eks-cluster \\\n  --profile xxxx\n\nAdded new context arn:aws:eks:ap-southeast-1:173310766280:cluster/hc-eks-cluster to /Users/k.sithi/.kube/config\n\nNote: The EKS endpoint is private. You need network access to the VPC (VPN, bastion, or Boundary worker) to run kubectl commands.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "After EKS is deployed, configure kubectl from a machine with VPC access (or via VPN/bastion):\n\n# Update kubeconfig (requires VPC network access)\naws eks update-kubeconfig \\\n  --region ap-southeast-1 \\\n  --name hc-eks-cluster \\\n  --profile xxxx\n\nAdded new context arn:aws:eks:ap-southeast-1:173310766280:cluster/hc-eks-cluster to /Users/k.sithi/.kube/config\n\nNote: The EKS endpoint is private. You need network access to the VPC (VPN, bastion, or Boundary worker) to run kubectl commands.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.2,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
